      },
      "output": "**Assumption:** You are a mechanical\u2011engineering student preparing for a thermodynamics final on the 20th and can dedicate\u202f\u2248\u202f3\u202fhours\u202fday\u207b\u00b9 to focused study.\n\n**Two\u2011week study schedule**\n\n| Day | Focus & Activities (\u22483\u202fh) |\n|-----|---------------------------|\n| 1 | Review lecture notes\u202f+\u202foutline the syllabus; list all major topics (laws, cycles, property tables). |\n| 2 | First law (energy balances) \u2013 work through a textbook example of a closed system; create a one\u2011page cheat sheet of key equations. |\n| 3 | Second law \u2013 entropy generation; solve a simple heat\u2011transfer problem; add entropy sign\u2011convention table to cheat sheet. |\n| 4 | Property relations \u2013 use steam tables/ Mollier diagram; practice interpolating values for two sample states. |\n| 5 | Ideal\u2011gas & real\u2011gas models \u2013 derive PV\u202f=\u202fnRT and apply the compressibility factor; solve a problem on gas expansion. |\n| 6 | Power cycles \u2013 Rankine cycle basics; draw the T\u2011s diagram and compute efficiency for a given set of boiler/condensor pressures. |\n| 7 | Refrigeration cycles \u2013 Vapor\u2011compression cycle; calculate COP for a sample refrigerator. |\n| 8 | Review days\u202f1\u20117 \u2013 quick flash\u2011card quiz on equations and concepts; identify any lingering weak spots. |\n| 9 | Combustion & chemical\u2011reaction thermochemistry \u2013 Hess\u2019s law example; compute enthalpy change for a fuel\u2011oxidation reaction. |\n| 10 | Irreversibility & exergy \u2013 solve an exergy\u2011destruction problem for a throttling valve. |\n| 11 | Multicomponent systems \u2013 partial molar properties; practice a mixture\u2011property calculation. |\n| 12 | Practice exam \u2013 attempt a past\u2011paper question set covering all topics; time yourself (\u224890\u202fmin). |\n| 13 | Review the practice exam \u2013 mark errors, revisit the specific concepts that caused mistakes, redo those problems. |\n| 14 | Final consolidation \u2013 rewrite the cheat sheet from memory, run a rapid \u201cclosed\u2011book\u201d recall of each major topic, and relax with light review (e.g., flash cards). |\n\n**Next step:** After you try Day\u202f12\u2019s practice set, let me know which topics gave you the most trouble so we can fine\u2011tune the final review.",
